Subject: [PATCH] Declare the poetry build backend

pyproject.toml has no [build-system] table, so PEP 518 falls back to
setuptools' legacy backend, which cannot read [tool.poetry]. Building that way
yields a wheel with no version and no entry points:

  Successfully installed checksumdir-0.0.0

__init__.py reads its own version back out of the installed metadata, so this
matters at runtime, not just cosmetically.

--- a/pyproject.toml	2026-10-02 15:22:45
+++ b/pyproject.toml	2026-10-02 15:22:56
@@ -30,4 +30,8 @@
 isort = "^5.13.0"
 
 [tool.poetry.scripts]
-checksumdir = 'checksumdir.cli:main'
\ No newline at end of file
+checksumdir = 'checksumdir.cli:main'
+
+[build-system]
+requires = ["poetry-core>=1.0.0"]
+build-backend = "poetry.core.masonry.api"
